allMinors -- returns all minors of one matroid in another
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        allMinors(M, N)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, the ambient matroid
      * N, a *note matroid: Matroid,, the candidate minor
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of pairs (S, T), such that M / S \ T
        is isomorphic to N

Description
===========

This method returns a list of all possible ways to realize N as a minor of M.
The output is a list of pairs (S, T) of subsets of the ground set of M such
that *note minor(M, S, T): minor, is isomorphic to N.

In fact, S will be an independent subset of M, of size = rank M - rank N, and T
will be a coindependent subset of M, of size = #((M/S).groundSet) -
#N.groundSet, which is disjoint from S.

The output of this method should be the empty list iff the output of *note
hasMinor: hasMinor, is false (for the same input).



+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : V = specificMatroid "vamos"                                 |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 4 on 8 elements                         |
|                                                                 |
|o1 : Matroid                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : U25 = uniformMatroid(2,5)                                   |
|                                                                 |
|o2 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 5 elements                         |
|                                                                 |
|o2 : Matroid                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : elapsedTime L = allMinors(V, U25);                          |
| -- .0536183s elapsed                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : #L                                                          |
|                                                                 |
|o4 = 64                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : netList L_{0..4}                                            |
|                                                                 |
|     +----------+-------+                                        |
|o5 = |set {5, 3}|set {2}|                                        |
|     +----------+-------+                                        |
|     |set {5, 3}|set {4}|                                        |
|     +----------+-------+                                        |
|     |set {6, 3}|set {2}|                                        |
|     +----------+-------+                                        |
|     |set {6, 3}|set {7}|                                        |
|     +----------+-------+                                        |
|     |set {5, 6}|set {0}|                                        |
|     +----------+-------+                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : all(L, pair -> areIsomorphic(U25, minor(V, pair#0, pair#1)))|
|                                                                 |
|o6 = true                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minor: minor, -- minor of matroid
  * *note hasMinor: hasMinor, -- whether a matroid has a given minor

Ways to use allMinors:
======================

  * "allMinors(Matroid,Matroid)"

