bases -- bases of matroid
*************************

  * Usage: 
        bases M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of bases

Description
===========

Returns a list of bases of the matroid. The basis elements are represented as
sets of nonnegative integers, which are the indices of the elements in the
ground set that make up a basis element. To get the subset of the ground set
corresponding to a set of indices, use *note subscripts: Matroid _us List,.



+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}})|
|                                         |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements |
|                                         |
|o1 : Matroid                             |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : bases M                             |
|                                         |
|o2 = {set {0, 1}, set {0, 2}}            |
|                                         |
|o2 : List                                |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : M_((bases M)#0)                     |
|                                         |
|o3 = set {a, b}                          |
|                                         |
|o3 : Set                                 |
+-----------------------------------------+



In this package, bases are the only structure that is always computed upon
creation of a matroid. Additional invariants (such as the *note ideal:
ideal_lpMatroid_rp, or *note circuits: circuits,) are not precomputed, but are
cached after being computed once. This allows for maximum speed in methods that
need to call the *note constructor function: matroid, many, many times: e.g.
*note tuttePolynomial: tuttePolynomial_lpMatroid_rp, and *note hasMinor:
hasMinor,.

See also
========

  * *note nonbases: nonbases, -- nonbases of matroid
  * *note independentSets(Matroid): independentSets_lpMatroid_cmZZ_rp, --
    independent subsets of a matroid
  * *note Matroid _ List: Matroid _us List, -- elements of matroid

Ways to use bases:
==================

  * "bases(Matroid)"

For the programmer
==================

