circuits -- circuits of matroid
*******************************

  * Usage: 
        circuits M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of circuits

Description
===========

The circuits of a matroid are the minimal dependent subsets of the ground set.

Just as with *note bases: bases, and *note nonbases: nonbases,, circuits are
stored via their indices (rather than the elements of the ground set
themselves).



+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}})|
|                                         |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements |
|                                         |
|o1 : Matroid                             |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : circuits M                          |
|                                         |
|o2 = {set {1, 2}, set {3}}               |
|                                         |
|o2 : List                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ideal(Matroid): ideal_lpMatroid_rp, -- Stanley-Reisner (circuit)
    ideal of matroid
  * *note fundamentalCircuit: fundamentalCircuit, -- fundamental circuit of
    independent set
