closure -- closure of a subset of a matroid
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        closure(M, S)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
      * S, a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, of indices, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of elements in M
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

The closure of a subset S of a matroid (E, B) is the set cl(S) := {x $\in$ E :
rank(S) = rank(S $\cup \{x\}$) }. The closure operator 2^E -> 2^E, S $\mapsto$
cl(S), completely determines the matroid (indeed, the maximal proper closed
sets - i.e. *note hyperplanes: hyperplanes, - already determine the matroid).



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}})                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Matroid                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : for s in subsets M_* do print(toString s | " has closure " | toString   |
|{} has closure {3}                                                           |
|{a} has closure {0, 3}                                                       |
|{b} has closure {1, 2, 3}                                                    |
|{a, b} has closure {0, 1, 2, 3}                                              |
|{c} has closure {1, 2, 3}                                                    |
|{a, c} has closure {0, 1, 2, 3}                                              |
|{b, c} has closure {1, 2, 3}                                                 |
|{a, b, c} has closure {0, 1, 2, 3}                                           |
|{d} has closure {3}                                                          |
|{a, d} has closure {0, 3}                                                    |
|{b, d} has closure {1, 2, 3}                                                 |
|{a, b, d} has closure {0, 1, 2, 3}                                           |
|{c, d} has closure {1, 2, 3}                                                 |
|{a, c, d} has closure {0, 1, 2, 3}                                           |
|{b, c, d} has closure {1, 2, 3}                                              |
|{a, b, c, d} has closure {0, 1, 2, 3}                                        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|closure_M s)                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = flats M                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {set {3}, set {1, 2, 3}, set {0, 3}, set {0, 1, 2, 3}}                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : all(F, f -> closure_M f === f)                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

