coloops -- coloops of matroid
*****************************

  * Usage: 
        coloops M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

The coloops of a matroid M are the loops of the *note dual: dual_lpMatroid_rp,
matroid. The set of coloops of M equals both the intersection of the *note
bases: bases, of M, and the complement of the union of the *note circuits:
circuits, of M.



+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}})                 |
|                                                          |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements                  |
|                                                          |
|o1 : Matroid                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : circuits M                                           |
|                                                          |
|o2 = {set {1, 2}, set {3}}                                |
|                                                          |
|o2 : List                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = set coloops M                                    |
|                                                          |
|o3 = set {0}                                              |
|                                                          |
|o3 : Set                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C === M.groundSet - fold(circuits M, (a, b) -> a + b)|
|                                                          |
|o4 = true                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C === fold(bases M, (a, b) -> a*b)                   |
|                                                          |
|o5 = true                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M_C                                                  |
|                                                          |
|o6 = set {a}                                              |
|                                                          |
|o6 : Set                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : D = dual M; peek D                                   |
|                                                          |
|o8 = Matroid{bases => {set {2, 3}, set {1, 3}}}           |
|             cache => CacheTable{...2...}                 |
|             groundSet => set {0, 1, 2, 3}                |
|             rank => 2                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : coloops matroid completeGraph 4 == {}                |
|                                                          |
|o9 = true                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note loops: loops, -- loops of matroid
  * *note dual(Matroid): dual_lpMatroid_rp, -- dual matroid

Ways to use coloops:
====================

  * "coloops(Matroid)"

For the programmer
==================

