contraction -- contraction of subset of matroid
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        contraction(M, S)
        M / S
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
      * S, a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, of indices, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of elements in M
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matroid: Matroid,, the contraction M / S

Description
===========

The contraction of M by S is given by M/S := (M* \ S)*, where * stands for
dual, and \ is deletion.



+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}}) |
|                                          |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements  |
|                                          |
|o1 : Matroid                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = M / {c}                          |
|                                          |
|o2 = a "matroid" of rank 1 on 3 elements  |
|                                          |
|o2 : Matroid                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek N                               |
|                                          |
|o3 = Matroid{bases => {set {0}}          }|
|             cache => CacheTable{...2...} |
|             groundSet => set {0, 1, 2}   |
|             rank => 1                    |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : N == M / set{2}                      |
|                                          |
|o4 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note deletion: deletion, -- deletion of subset of matroid
  * *note dual(Matroid): dual_lpMatroid_rp, -- dual matroid
  * *note minor: minor, -- minor of matroid

