flats -- flats of a matroid
***************************

  * Usage: 
        flats M
        flats(M, r)
        flats(M, r, s)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a target (co)rank (optional)
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, either "rank" or "corank"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

A flat, or closed subset, of a matroid is a subset A of the ground set which
equals its *note closure: closure,. The set of flats, partially ordered by
inclusion, forms a lattice, called the *note lattice of flats: latticeOfFlats,.
This is an important invariant of the matroid: one can recover the matroid from
the lattice of flats, and for simple matroids (i.e. matroids whose circuits all
have size >= 3), the isomorphism type of the lattice is already a complete
invariant.

If a target rank r is provided, then this method returns the list of all rank r
flats of M.

If a target corank r is provided along with the mode "corank", then this method
computes all intersections of r distinct hyperplanes. This is guaranteed to
contain all flats of rank = rank M - r (cf. Oxley, Prop. 1.7.8), and may be
useful if the lattice of flats is large, and only the upper portion is required
(such as in the Scum theorem).



