fVector(Matroid) -- f-vector of a matroid
*****************************************

  * Function: *note fVector: (Polyhedra)fVector,
  * Usage: 
        fVector M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, 

Description
===========

The f-vector of a matroid M is the invariant (f_0, f_1, ..., f_r), where f_i is
the number of *note rank: rank_lpMatroid_cmSet_rp, i *note flats: flats, of M,
and r is the *note rank: rank_lpMatroid_rp, of M. Note that f_0 = f_r = 1, as
the set of *note loops: loops, is the unique flat of rank 0, and the ground set
is the unique flat of maximal rank.



+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}})|
|                                         |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements |
|                                         |
|o1 : Matroid                             |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : fVector M                           |
|                                         |
|o2 = HashTable{0 => 1}                   |
|               1 => 2                    |
|               2 => 1                    |
|                                         |
|o2 : HashTable                           |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : fVector matroid completeGraph 4     |
|                                         |
|o3 = HashTable{0 => 1}                   |
|               1 => 6                    |
|               2 => 7                    |
|               3 => 1                    |
|                                         |
|o3 : HashTable                           |
+-----------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This is not the same as the f-vector of the *note independence complex:
independenceComplex_lpMatroid_rp, of the matroid M, which counts the number of
independent sets of a given size. To do this instead, use "fVector
independenceComplex M".

See also
========

  * *note flats: flats, -- flats of a matroid
  * *note rank(Matroid): rank_lpMatroid_rp, -- rank of a matroid
  * *note latticeOfFlats: latticeOfFlats, -- lattice of flats of a matroid

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note fVector(Matroid): fVector_lpMatroid_rp, -- f-vector of a matroid
