hyperplanes -- hyperplanes of a matroid
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        hyperplanes M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

The hyperplanes of a matroid are the flats of rank equal to rank M - 1. The
complements of the hyperplanes are precisely the *note circuits: circuits, of
the *note dual: dual_lpMatroid_rp, matroid (which is indeed how this method
computes hyperplanes), and thus a matroid is determined by its hyperplanes.



+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}})|
|                                         |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements |
|                                         |
|o1 : Matroid                             |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : hyperplanes M                       |
|                                         |
|o2 = {set {1, 2, 3}, set {0, 3}}         |
|                                         |
|o2 : List                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

