idealChowRing -- the defining ideal of the Chow ring
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        idealChowRing M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ChowRingOptions => ..., default value new OptionTable from
        {MonomialOrder => GLex}
      * CoefficientRing => ..., default value QQ
      * FlatOrder => ..., default value null
      * Presentation => ..., default value "standard"
      * Variable => ..., default value "x"
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the defining ideal of the Chow
        ring of M

Description
===========

The Chow ring of M is the ring R := QQ[x_F]/(I1 + I2), where $I1 =
(\sum_{i_1\in F} x_F - \sum_{i_2\in F} x_F : i_1, i_2 \in M)$ and $I2 =
(x_Fx_{F'} : F, F' incomparable)$, as $F$ runs over all proper nonempty flats
of $M$. This is the same as the Chow ring of the toric variety associated to
the Bergman fan of M. This ring is an Artinian standard graded Gorenstein ring,
by a result of Adiprasito, Katz, and Huh: cf. https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.02888,
Theorem 6.19.

This method returns the defining ideal of the Chow ring, which lives in a
polynomial ring with variable indices equal to the flats of M. To work with
these subscripts, use "last baseName v" to get the index of a variable v. For
more information, cf. *note Working with Chow rings of matroids: Working with
Chow rings of matroids,.



