independenceComplex(Matroid) -- independence complex of matroid
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note independenceComplex: (Graphs)independenceComplex,
  * Usage: 
        independenceComplex M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex:
        (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,,

Description
===========

The independence complex of a matroid is the simplicial complex associated (via
the Stanley-Reisner correspondence) to the circuit ideal of the matroid (which
is a squarefree monomial ideal). This method uses the *note
SimplicialComplexes: (SimplicialComplexes)Top, package to return an object of
type *note SimplicialComplex: (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,.



+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({{0,1},{0,2},{0,3},{1,2},{2,3}})            |
|                                                             |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements                     |
|                                                             |
|o1 : Matroid                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : independenceComplex M                                   |
|                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | x_2x_3 x_0x_3 x_1x_2 x_0x_2 x_0x_1 ||
|                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

