independentSets(Matroid,ZZ) -- independent subsets of a matroid
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note independentSets: (Macaulay2Doc)independentSets,
  * Usage: 
        independentSets(M, s)
        independentSets M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Limit: (Macaulay2Doc)independentSets, => ..., default value
        infinity,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of independent sets in M

Description
===========

A subset of the ground set is called independent if it is contained in a *note
basis: bases,, or equivalently, does not contain a *note circuit: circuits,.
This method returns certain independent subsets of the ground set, depending on
the input:

If an integer $s$ is provided, then all independent subsets of size $s$ in $M$
are returned.

If a subset $S$ of the ground set of $M$ is given, then all maximal independent
subsets of $S$ are returned.

If neither a size $s$ nor a subset $S$ is given, then all independent sets of M
is returned (which may be quite large).



