restriction -- restriction to subset of matroid
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        restriction(M, S)
        M | S
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matroid: Matroid,, 
      * S, a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, of indices, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of elements in M
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matroid: Matroid,, the restriction M | S

Description
===========

The restriction of M to S, M | S, has ground set S and independent sets equal
to the independent sets of M contained in S.



+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matroid({a,b,c,d},{{a,b},{a,c}}) |
|                                          |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 4 elements  |
|                                          |
|o1 : Matroid                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = M | {a,b,d}                      |
|                                          |
|o2 = a "matroid" of rank 2 on 3 elements  |
|                                          |
|o2 : Matroid                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek N                               |
|                                          |
|o3 = Matroid{bases => {set {0, 1}}       }|
|             cache => CacheTable{...1...} |
|             groundSet => set {0, 1, 2}   |
|             rank => 2                    |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : N == M | set{0,1,3}                  |
|                                          |
|o4 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

