thetaMatroid -- theta matroid
*****************************

  * Usage: 
        M = thetaMatroid n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matroid: Matroid,, the theta matroid

Description
===========

The family of theta matroids appears in Oxley, p. 663. For a given n,
thetaMatroid n has 2n elements and rank n.

A notable feature of this family is that thetaMatroid n is representable over a
field iff the field has at least n - 1 elements (a property also shared by
uniformMatroid(2, n)).



+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = thetaMatroid 3                       |
|                                              |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 3 on 6 elements      |
|                                              |
|o1 : Matroid                                  |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : areIsomorphic(M, matroid completeGraph 4)|
|                                              |
|o2 = true                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+

