wheel -- wheels/whirls
**********************

  * Usage: 
        M = wheel r
        M = whirl r
  * Inputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matroid: Matroid,, a rank r wheel or whirl

Description
===========

The families of wheels and whirls appears in Oxley, p. 659-660. The rank-r
wheel is the graphic matroid of the *note wheel graph: (Graphs)wheelGraph, with
r outer vertices, and has 2r elements. The rank-r whirl is the unique
relaxation of the rank-r wheel (and thus also has 2r elements).



+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = wheel 3                        |
|                                        |
|o1 = a "matroid" of rank 3 on 6 elements|
|                                        |
|o1 : Matroid                            |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : M == matroid wheelGraph 4          |
|                                        |
|o2 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = whirl 3                        |
|                                        |
|o3 = a "matroid" of rank 3 on 6 elements|
